          "analysis": "This binary is the legitimate Microsoft Windows File System Conversion Utility (convert.exe). The analysis shows it is designed to convert disk volumes from one file system to another (typically FAT32 to NTFS). The decompiled code reveals standard command-line argument parsing (e.g., /FS, /V, /X, /NoSecurity) and the use of the IFSUTIL library to interact with disk structures. It schedules conversion tasks to run at boot time using the 'autocheck autoconv' mechanism, which is a standard Windows behavior for system utilities requiring exclusive disk access. No malicious behavior or suspicious IOCs were identified.",
